.Dd May 27, 2026
.Dt ORACLECTL 8
.Os
.Sh NAME
.Nm oraclectl
.Nd control interface for oracled
.Sh SYNOPSIS
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm status
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm shutdown
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm reload
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm kldload Ar module
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm kldunload Ar module
.Nm
.Op Fl s Ar socket
.Cm reboot
.Sh DESCRIPTION
.Nm
sends administrative commands to a running
.Xr oracled 8
instance via its control socket.
.Pp
The
.Fl s
option specifies an alternate socket path (default:
.Pa /var/run/oracled.sock ) .
This is needed when
.Xr oracled 8
is configured with a non-default
.Va control_socket
path.
Each invocation connects, sends a single command, prints the
result, and exits.
.Pp
The following commands are available:
.Bl -tag -width "kldunload module"
.It Cm status
Query the daemon's status and uptime.
This command does not require root privileges.
.It Cm shutdown
Request a graceful shutdown of
.Xr oracled 8 .
The daemon terminates its process subtree, releases all capability
runtime resources, and exits.
Requires root.
.It Cm reload
Request a configuration reload.
Requires root.
.It Cm kldload Ar module
Load a kernel module through
.Xr oracled 8 .
The module is loaded by the daemon process, which may hold
privileges or isolation claims that the caller does not.
Requires root.
.It Cm kldunload Ar module
Unload a kernel module through
.Xr oracled 8 .
Requires root.
.It Cm reboot
Initiate a system reboot through
.Xr oracled 8 .
The daemon performs a graceful shutdown before rebooting.
Requires root.
.El
.Sh EXIT STATUS
.Ex -std
.Pp
Privileged commands return
.Er EX_NOPERM
when executed by a non-root user.
If
.Xr oracled 8
is not running,
.Nm
exits with
.Er EX_UNAVAILABLE .
.Sh FILES
.Bl -tag -width "/var/run/oracled.sock"
.It Pa /var/run/oracled.sock
Unix domain socket used to communicate with
.Xr oracled 8 .
.El
.Sh SEE ALSO
.Xr kldload 8 ,
.Xr oracled 8 ,
.Xr reboot 8
.Sh HISTORY
.Nm
first appeared in 5BSD.
